        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive specification developed for our audit team's procedures when clients rely on third-party service organizations as part of their financial reporting information systems, specifically in the context of integrated audits of internal control over financial reporting under PCAOB AS 2201. The spec should address how to identify when a service organization's activities are part of the client's information system, how to apply the relevant concepts from AS 2601 in the ICFR audit context, and what documentation standards apply. Additionally, please incorporate guidance on how to handle situations where management's disclosures about scope limitations related to service organizations are inadequate\u2014specifically, the communication responsibilities to management and the audit committee modeled on the interim review communication requirements in AS 4105 paragraphs 29 through 32, and the requirement to add an explanatory paragraph to the ICFR audit report if management and the audit committee fail to respond appropriately. The spec should cover the full workflow from initial scoping of service organization reliance through final report modification, and we need it ready for partner review before we kick off next quarter's engagement cycle.",
